This is the NEWS file for RCC, the Regoshi C Compiler. It summarizes
user-visible changes for each release, most recent first. For the
complete list of changes see the git log.

* Changes in v1.2.2 (2026-09-19) (Reini Urban)

  - New -O1 codegen passes: local value propagation with dead-store
    elimination, jump threading, cheap algebraic-identity folds, and
    dense small-int switch → jump table lowering. Sparse switches
    (>=150 exact-value cases, benchmarked breakeven) now lower to a
    balanced binary search or a perfect-hash dispatch instead of a
    linear cmp/jcc chain.
  - New -O2 single-scalar-arg/return tail-call optimization on
    x86-64 and ARM64 (ND_RETURN tail-jmp under -finline+-funroll),
    with frame-escape and __builtin_* safety checks.
  - Added FreeBSD, NetBSD and OpenBSD support, all three built and
    tested in CI (vmactions QEMU VMs) as mandatory, blocking jobs —
    no `continue-on-error`. Also added a `clang`-built matrix job on
    Linux (rcc itself is compiler-agnostic; only the build toolchain
    changes).
  - Fixed a real, universal codegen bug found via FreeBSD CI: an
    `extern __thread` variable owned by a separate shared library
    (e.g. libc's own TLS state, reached through an inlined libc
    header) got the unsafe direct-offset (local-exec) TLS
    relocation, valid only for TLS vars owned by the same link unit.
    Now uses the GOT-indirected initial-exec model whenever the
    variable is extern/weak, on every platform.
  - Fixed a real ELF-writer bug found via OpenBSD/FreeBSD CI (both
    use LLVM's `ld.lld` as the system linker): a SHF_MERGE section's
    on-disk size wasn't padded to a multiple of its declared
    `sh_entsize`, which the ELF spec requires and `ld.lld` correctly
    enforces (`ld.bfd` silently tolerates the violation, masking it
    on Linux). Affected real code, e.g. the Linux kernel's
    `ALTERNATIVE()` macro's `.altinstructions` table.
  - Fixed undefined behavior in the lexer: `isspace`/`isdigit`/
    `isxdigit`/`ispunct` were called on signed `char` values instead
    of `(unsigned char)`, undefined for any UTF-8 byte ≥0x80. glibc
    tolerates it silently; NetBSD's stricter libc didn't, crashing
    on any non-ASCII identifier.
  - Fixed a test-harness crash (not rcc itself) on NetBSD: a
    diagnostic re-run path passed a literal NULL as `argv[0]` to
    `posix_spawnp()`, which NetBSD's libc dereferences and segfaults
    on.
  - rcc's native ELF linker falls back to the system `cc`/`ld` on
    every BSD for cases it doesn't special-case yet (BSD `crt1.o`
    layout, `PT_INTERP`/`DT_NEEDED` naming) — tracked in `TODO`.

* Changes in v1.2.1 (2026-09-16) (Reini Urban)

  - Compile-time performance: faster lexer (ASCII fast path), faster
    linker (indexed/DT_HASH symbol lookups instead of rescanning
    .dynsym per symbol), faster preprocessor (concat_strings() relinks
    tokens instead of cloning the stream); better benchmarks
  - Added test/gcc-bugs/, a suite of ~600 reproducers for GCC's open
    bug tracker.
  - Fixed a parser segfault on sizeof() with unbalanced parens and
    several further gcc-bugs regressions (const-init, vector_size,
    enum attribute, atomic pointer, __has_builtin, alignas).
  - Implemented sqrt() on a vector-of-2-doubles, 3 missing GCC
    diagnostics, duplicate-function-definition detection, and the GCC
    extension accepting a missing ';' at the end of a struct/union.
  - New optimizations: generalized AST constant folding covers
    bitwise/shift/compare/unary/?: on compile-time constants (not
    just `+ - * / %`); do-while(0) macro-body flattening at -O1+;
    and a new src/cg_opt.c does x86-64/ARM64 constant-divisor
    idiv/div strength reduction (shifts and Hacker's Delight/LLVM
    magic-number multiplies) for signed and unsigned 32/64-bit
    division and modulo.
  - Added csmith differential fuzzing diffing -O0/-O1/-O2/-O3 codegen
    against each other and reference compilers. Found and fixed 9 register-
    allocator/spiller aliasing miscompilations (struct-copy and
    struct-assign, ternary and pre/post-increment addressing,
    bitfield read-modify-write, cmp-lhs and %rsi clobbers across
    gen_funcall argument staging, Win64 variadic frame overflow,
    ARM64 global-load aliasing, register-pressure undercounting),
    each with a regression test under test/test_csmith_*.c.
  - Fixed 3 -O2-only regressions found by bisecting the full -O2
    suite (try_inline() signedness mismatch, try_unroll() early-exit
    induction-variable value, float-to-int cast saturation
    mismatch), plus a _Complex comparison register leak in
    gen_cond_branch_inv.
  - Fixed ND_ASSIGN narrow-type truncation and array-not-assignable
    diagnostics, a pack(1) bitfield global-initializer truncation
    past 4 bytes, and an overflowing snprintf() call.
  - Fixed libdir lookup with installed rcc. Fixed arm64-elf GOT
    load for extern function address-of.
  - Faster `make install` (only reinstalls changed files). Test
    harness: run_tests --timeout now also bounds the compiler
    process, per-compiler timeouts and --no-<compiler> skip flags
    for test-all-compilers.sh, rv-match kcc and blitzy/ccc-fork
    support, and a gnulib-style news-check + mk-release release
    tool.

* Changes in v1.2.0 (2026-09-04) (Reini Urban)

  - New linux/elf x86_64 and darwin-aarch64 backends, native
    assembler and linker.
  - Also a much faster preprocessor, which doesn't retokenize, but
    dumps the pp tokens only on -E to a string.
  - New test suites from ncc, c-testsuite and gcc torture, running in
    parallel. Also many more unit-tests for all fixed bugs.
  - New bench suites for middle sized, and larged sized code.
  - Fixed all the bugs, and added all C23 and C29 features.
  - Added a comprehensive C compiler test overview table.
  - Compiles the linux kernel and all ~270 slimcc third_party test
    projects.
  - Compiled code is slower, but more correct than with all other
    compilers. And it compiles almost as fast as tinycc, with just
    much more features.

